1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,950
One spoonful of this honey
makes the world melt.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,200
And it once stopped an army.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:08,800
In Nepal, the world's largest bee

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,700
nests on three-hundred-foot cliffs.

5
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,550
It feeds on poisonous
rhododendron flowers.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,600
So its honey carries
a real neurotoxin.

7
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,950
Small dose? Your body burns.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,250
The room spins.

9
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:22,900
Too much... and your
heart slows down.

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,000
Around 65 BC,

11
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,550
locals left bowls of it
for Roman soldiers.

12
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:29,400
One thousand never got up.

13
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:32,100
Hunters still climb for it,
barehanded.

14
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,850
One jar: two hundred dollars.

15
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:36,300
Would you taste it?
